diff --git a/docs/decisions/2977-agie-die-pair.md b/docs/decisions/2977-agie-die-pair.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..e249a8505
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/decisions/2977-agie-die-pair.md
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+## #2977 - Two through-openings in one native Agie die job
+
+**Decided.** Match each selected rim to an opening in the same modeled plate. Require exactly two openings and two disjoint compensated cutting and threading areas. Keep each work's threading point, inward cut side, capture and separation.
+
+**Why.** The two operations protect the same retained material. Matching each selected boundary against the complete vertical prism checks that the cut goes through the plate. Disjoint envelopes require the operations to use different openings and leave a clear band between their cuts.
+
+**Alternatives and cost.** Mixed punch and die work would need interference checks against the entire retained die plate. Additional openings would need complete one-to-one rim matching, clearance checks between every pair and verification of the controller's release sequence. Both extensions can use the same resource map after those checks exist.
diff --git a/docs/user-guide/agie-wire-edm.md b/docs/user-guide/agie-wire-edm.md
index 55a0b5e1f..eb5441219 100644
--- a/docs/user-guide/agie-wire-edm.md
+++ b/docs/user-guide/agie-wire-edm.md
@@ -36,6 +36,18 @@ cargo run -p camcraft-app --bin camcraft-cli -- script examples/agie/die-plate.c
 
 The example selects the complete upper opening rim on a 60 × 60 mm plate. The native `DIE20` job starts at X−5.5 Y0 and enters the straight wall at X−12.5 Y0. Inspect the **inside** compensation and the 1 mm rough separation in Agie Control. The controller completes the separation before it makes the three full trim passes. Arrange support for the slug and a clear trim path after release.
 
+### Group two die openings in one plate
+
+Use one retained plate with exactly two through-openings, one setup, 20 mm stock and the same **AGIE_QN2** wire condition for both operations. Create one **Wire Contour** for each opening. Select each opening's upper rim, enter its own threading hole and confirm capture for its slug. Leave a clear band along X or Y between the two cutting areas, including the leads and wire clearance. Generate both operations and post to a new job folder with a name of up to seven characters.
+
+Run the original two-opening example from the project root.
+
+```sh
+cargo run -p camcraft-app --bin camcraft-cli -- script examples/agie/die-pair.camscript
+```
+
+The `DUODI20` folder contains two ISO files, one SBR and one SBL. The left work threads at X−35.5 Y0. The right work threads at X24.5 Y0. Check each inward offset and the release of both slugs in the control preview before running the job.
+
 ### QN2 offsets by stock thickness
 
 Agie Control calculated these wire-centre offsets on the straight outside faces of a synthetic rectangular punch. All dimensions are in millimetres. The native job sends nominal geometry. The resident technology applies each offset.
diff --git a/examples/agie/die-pair.camscript b/examples/agie/die-pair.camscript
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..8472e06b5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/examples/agie/die-pair.camscript
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+// Original CAMCraft example. Run from the project root with a fresh output name.
+cam.call("load_machine", {builtin: "AGIECUT Classic 2S (template)"});
+cam.call("edit_machine", {patch: {edm: {conditions: [{
+  id: "AGIE_QN2", role: "rough", gap: 0.005, wire_diameter: 0.25
+}]}}});
+cam.call("add_tool", {catalog: "EDM-W025"});
+cam.import("examples/agie/die-pair.obj", "plate");
+cam.call("set_stock", {box: {dx: 130, dy: 70, dz: 20}});
+cam.call("set_wcs", {origin: [0, 0, 20]});
+const features = cam.call("list_features", {model: "plate", kinds: ["faces", "chains"]});
+const top = features.faces.find(face => face.facing === "up");
+const holes = top.loops.filter(loop => loop.kind === "hole" && loop.complete);
+for (const op of [{name: "DieL", x: -35.5}, {name: "DieR", x: 24.5}]) {
+  const rim = holes.find(loop => {
+    const edge = features.chains.find(chain => chain.id === loop.chains[0]);
+    return (edge.start[0] < 0) === (op.x < 0);
+  });
+  cam.call("add_operation", {
+    kind: "Wire Contour", name: op.name, source: "plate", tool: "EDM-W025",
+    params: {top_z: 20, bottom_z: 0, side: "die", condition: "AGIE_QN2",
+      start: [op.x, 0], capture: true}
+  });
+  cam.call("set_operation_geometry", {operation: op.name,
+    picks: rim.chains.map(id => ({model: "plate", id: id}))
+  });
+}
+cam.generate();
+cam.post({to: "DUODI20", cps: "Agie native wire EDM", options: {separationLengthMm: 1.0}});
